    <bpmn:process id="W_W68" name="W68. Product Lifecycle &amp; Discontinuation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly assortment review (W1) identifies SKUs for discontinuation; or vendor announces product end-of-life; or category rationalization decision
Frequency: ~4–8 discontinuation campaigns/year (aligned with W1 quarterly cycles); ~200–500 SKUs discontinued per campaign
Volume: ~1,000–2,000 SKUs discontinued/year (balanced by ~1,500–2,500 new SKUs/year from W1/W32); each SKU follows the same lifecycle
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Buyer, Merchandise Planner, Pricing Analyst, Supply Planner, Marketing, Store Operations
Source: workflow W68 — Product Lifecycle &amp; Discontinuation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W68_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W68_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task21</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W68_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W68_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W68_Lane4" name="Supply Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W68_Lane5" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task20</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W68_Lane6" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W68_Lane7" name="AP Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_Task19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W68_End22</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W68_Start9" name="Quarterly assortment review (W1) identifies SKUs for discontinuation; or vendor announces…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task10" name="Category Manager identifies SKUs for discontinuation from W1.2 underperformer…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Category Manager identifies SKUs for discontinuation from W1.2 underperformer analysis (bottom 10% by revenue/sqm, negative margin, &lt; 2 turns/year, or vendor product end-of-life notification); creates discontinuation candidate list per category
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task11" name="Buyer validates discontinuation impact per SKU: (a) remaining open POs — can…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Buyer validates discontinuation impact per SKU: (a) remaining open POs — can they be cancelled or reduced?, (b) outstanding vendor commitments on blanket POs (W2C) — minimum commitment status, (c) active rebate agreements (W27) — impact on rebate tier achievement, (d) vendor relationship impact — is vendor sole-source for other SKUs?
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 3 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task12" name="VP Merchandising approves discontinuation list; system sets &quot;Discontinued —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: VP Merchandising approves discontinuation list; system sets &quot;Discontinued — Pending&quot; status on approved SKUs
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task13" name="Last buy decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Last buy decision: for each discontinued SKU, Buyer determines: (a) cancel all open POs (standard action) or (b) place final buy order to cover estimated sell-through during clearance period if remaining stock is critically low and sufficient margin exists; final buy follows standard W2A PO process but flagged as &quot;Last Buy&quot; — no future auto-replenishment
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task14" name="Supply Planner disables auto-replenishment (ROP) for discontinued SKUs; system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Supply Planner disables auto-replenishment (ROP) for discontinued SKUs; system stops generating suggested POs; remaining store replenishment continues until DC stock is exhausted; system auto-cancels all open backorders (W56) for discontinued SKUs across all stores; customers with cancelled backorders notified via SMS/email with apology and option to select a substitute item (directed to Sales Associate or CSR for assistance)
Responsible (R): Supply Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 30 min/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task15" name="Merchandise Planner flags SKU as &quot;Discontinued&quot; in item master with effective…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Merchandise Planner flags SKU as &quot;Discontinued&quot; in item master with effective date; item hidden from planogram tools and new store assortment assignments (W16.5); item remains visible in POS and ecommerce for selling remaining stock
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task16" name="Clearance execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Clearance execution: Pricing Analyst sets clearance markdown per W13.9a — system applies clearance price at POS and ecommerce; POS displays clearance disclaimer; Dept. Supervisors move items to clearance section; clearance period typically 4–6 weeks (longer than promo clearance per W13.9a to allow complete sell-through)
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst / Dept. Supervisor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow32</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task17" name="Weekly sell-through monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Weekly sell-through monitoring: Pricing Analyst reviews discontinued SKU sell-through dashboard; if sell-through rate &lt; 20% of remaining stock after 3 weeks, escalates to Category Manager for deeper markdown or accelerated disposition
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/week during clearance</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow32</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow33</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task18" name="Post-clearance disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-clearance disposition: at end of clearance period, remaining stock dispositioned per priority: (a) Return to Vendor (RTV) — Buyer coordinates per W3.6a, negotiate credit note; (b) bulk liquidation to discount buyers — Buyer arranges sale; (c) donation to partner organizations (Habitat for Humanity, local community organizations); (d) scrap/recycle — DC Supervisor authorizes per W3.6c; system removes remaining inventory and posts final loss
Responsible (R): Buyer / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow33</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow34</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task19" name="Vendor settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 10: Vendor settlement: AP Clerk processes any vendor credit memos from RTV per W7.9b; Buyer confirms vendor agreement termination or continued relationship on other SKUs; system releases any remaining blanket PO commitments per W2C
Responsible (R): AP Clerk / Buyer
Accountable (A): AP Supervisor
Duration: 1 hour/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow34</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow35</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task20" name="System archival">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 11: System archival: Merchandise Planner sets SKU status to &quot;Discontinued — Inactive&quot;; item removed from active search in POS (no longer scannable for new sales), removed from ecommerce catalog, excluded from inventory reports; item master record retained for 10 years per BIR retention (historical transaction references remain accessible); WAC and inventory value zeroed out
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow35</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow36</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W68_Task21" name="Post-discontinuation review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 12: Post-discontinuation review: Category Manager compares actual recovery rate (clearance + RTV credits) vs. write-off loss; documents learnings for future discontinuation decisions; feeds into quarterly assortment review (W1)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/campaign</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow36</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W68_Flow37</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W68_End22" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W68_Flow37</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W68_Annotation23">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
