    <bpmn:process id="W_W102" name="W102. Category Performance Review &amp; P&amp;L Ownership" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly category P&amp;L review calendar (5th business day of following month)
Frequency: Monthly review; quarterly deep-dive aligned with W1 assortment review
Volume: 13 product categories across 200 stores + 4 DCs; reviewed by 5 Category Managers
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Category Manager, Pricing Analyst, Buyer, Cost Accountant, VP Merchandising, VP Store Operations
Source: workflow W102 — Category Performance Review &amp; P&amp;L Ownership</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W102_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W102_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W102_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W102_Lane3" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W102_Lane4" name="Cost Accountant">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W102_Lane5" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W102_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W102_Start7" name="Monthly category P&amp;L review calendar (5th business day of following month)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W102_Task8" name="Revenue">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System generates monthly category P&amp;L report per category (and per Category Manager, covering 2–3 categories each): (a) Revenue: gross sales, returns, net sales — by store, by channel (in-store, ecommerce, B2B), by SKU count, (b) COGS: cost of goods sold at WAC, inbound freight allocation, landed cost adjustments, (c) Gross Margin: gross margin $ and % — vs. budget (W26) and vs. prior year, (d) Markdowns &amp; Clearance: total markdown value, markdown % of revenue — by reason (seasonal, slow-mover, damaged, promotional), per W93, (e) Shrinkage: inventory loss by category from W92 shrinkage report, (f) Net Margin: gross margin − markdowns − shrinkage = contribution margin by category, (g) Inventory Productivity: inventory turns, weeks of supply, GMROI (Gross Margin Return on Inventory Investment), sell-through %, (h) Vendor Performance: on-time delivery %, fill rate %, quality reject rate for top vendors in category per W44
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated (nightly batch, available T+3 business days)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W102_Task9" name="Category Manager reviews their category P&amp;L and prepares analysis: (a) identify…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager reviews their category P&amp;L and prepares analysis: (a) identify top 3 positive and top 3 negative variance drivers vs. budget, (b) explain margin erosion or improvement (cost changes from W40, promotional impact from W13, markdown impact from W93), (c) highlight store-level outliers (top 5 and bottom 5 stores by category margin), (d) identify SKUs with significant margin decline (cost up but SRP not adjusted per W40), (e) assess inventory productivity — categories with declining turns or excess weeks of supply need action plan
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–4 hours/category/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W102_Task10" name="Pricing Analyst provides supporting analysis: (a) price elasticity observations…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Pricing Analyst provides supporting analysis: (a) price elasticity observations from recent W40 price changes, (b) promotional ROI from recent W13 events, (c) competitive pricing benchmarking updates, (d) quantity break utilization from W40.19
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W102_Task11" name="Cost Accountant provides: (a) WAC verification per category (any unusual WAC…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cost Accountant provides: (a) WAC verification per category (any unusual WAC movements from import FX, landed cost adjustments), (b) intercompany margin impact (if category products flow through IC per W14), (c) NRV (Net Realizable Value) review for slow-moving categories per W9A.16b
Responsible (R): Cost Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W102_Task12" name="Category Manager presents category P&amp;L review to VP Merchandising in monthly…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Category Manager presents category P&amp;L review to VP Merchandising in monthly category review meeting (30–45 min per category): (a) performance summary — did the category meet revenue, margin, and inventory targets?, (b) variance explanations with root cause, (c) action plan for underperforming areas (pricing adjustment per W40, assortment change per W1, vendor negotiation, markdown acceleration per W93, replenishment parameter adjustment per W31.8), (d) forward-looking outlook — upcoming seasonal factors, promotional plans, vendor cost changes
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30–45 min/category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W102_Task13" name="VP Merchandising and Category Manager agree on action items with owners and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: VP Merchandising and Category Manager agree on action items with owners and deadlines; system tracks action items to closure
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 10 min/category</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W102_Task14" name="Quarterly (aligned with W1): deeper analysis including (a) category…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Quarterly (aligned with W1): deeper analysis including (a) category contribution to total company P&amp;L, (b) category market share analysis (if data available), (c) competitive category benchmarking, (d) SKU rationalization opportunities (further depth beyond W1), (e) vendor portfolio review for category (continue, expand, reduce, or exit vendor relationships per W44)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/category/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W102_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W102_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W102_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W102_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W102_Assoc17" sourceRef="W102_Annotation16" targetRef="W102_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
