    <bpmn:process id="W_W279" name="W279. Product Substitution Rules &amp; Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer orders a product (B2B, Ecommerce, or Endless Aisle) that is out of stock, prompting the system to offer an equivalent.
Frequency: Daily
Volume: 50-100 occurrences per day
Owner: Category Manager
Participants: Merchandising Admin, Ecommerce Ops, B2B Sales, Head of Trade / Account Management
Source: workflow W279 — Product Substitution Rules &amp; Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W279_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W279_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W279_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W279_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W279_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W279_Lane2" name="Merchandising Admin">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W279_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W279_Lane3" name="Ecommerce Ops">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W279_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W279_Lane4" name="B2B Sales">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W279_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W279_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W279_Start6" name="Customer orders a product (B2B, Ecommerce, or Endless Aisle) that is out of stock…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W279_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W279_Task7" name="Category Manager defines substitution chains in the ERP (e.g., if Brand A 2x4…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Category Manager defines substitution chains in the ERP (e.g., if Brand A 2x4 Lumber is out, substitute with Brand B); specifies equivalent items by attribute match (material, dimensions, performance grade).
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W279_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W279_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W279_Task8" name="Merchandising Admin configures price inheritance rules in the system (e.g…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Merchandising Admin configures price inheritance rules in the system (e.g., substitute item adopts the lower price, or requires customer approval if higher); sets substitution priority ranking for items with multiple substitutes.
Responsible (R): Merchandising Admin
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W279_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W279_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W279_Task9" name="During an online checkout or B2B order entry, the system auto-suggests the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: During an online checkout or B2B order entry, the system auto-suggests the substitute if inventory is zero; Ecommerce Ops reviews and tests substitution suggestions on the ecommerce platform for customer-facing accuracy.
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W279_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W279_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W279_Task10" name="Picker/Sales rep confirms the substitution at the store level or B2B order…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Picker/Sales rep confirms the substitution at the store level or B2B order desk; B2B Sales validates the substitute meets the customer&#x27;s technical requirements before confirming.
Responsible (R): B2B Sales
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W279_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W279_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W279_Task11" name="System tracks substitution metrics (substitution rate, acceptance rate, revenue…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: System tracks substitution metrics (substitution rate, acceptance rate, revenue recovery) to inform future demand forecasting, ensuring the original out-of-stock item&#x27;s forecast is adjusted.
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W279_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W279_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W279_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W279_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
