    <bpmn:process id="W_W625" name="W625. Product Quality Lab Testing &amp; Certification Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New product received at DC; periodic quality audit schedule; customer quality complaint
Frequency: Daily at DC receiving; weekly for ongoing batches; monthly for certification tracking
Volume: ~15–20 lab tests/month for high-risk categories (paint, electrical, adhesives, lumber treatment); ~50–80 certification verifications/month
Owner: Quality Assurance Manager
Participants: QA Manager, QA Lab Technician, Buyer, Category Manager, vendor quality representative
Source: workflow W625 — Product Quality Lab Testing &amp; Certification Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W625_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W625_Lane1" name="QA Lab Technician">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W625_Lane2" name="QA Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W625_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W625_Start4" name="New product received at DC; periodic quality audit schedule; customer quality complaint">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task5" name="QA Lab Technician receives test sample at DC quality lab — triggered by: (a)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: QA Lab Technician receives test sample at DC quality lab — triggered by: (a) new vendor first shipment (mandatory per W620), (b) periodic batch testing (quarterly for A-items in paint, electrical, adhesives), (c) customer quality complaint escalation (per W507), (d) random surveillance testing
Responsible (R): QA Lab Technician
Accountable (A): QA Manager
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task6" name="Paint">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: QA Lab Technician conducts product-specific testing per test protocol: (a) Paint: viscosity, drying time, color accuracy, volatile organic compound (VOC) levels per DENR standards, (b) Electrical: insulation resistance, conductor gauge verification, IP rating, safety mark verification per DTI-BPS (per W447), (c) Adhesives: bond strength, curing time, chemical composition, (d) Lumber treatment: preservative penetration depth, retention level per FPA standards
Responsible (R): QA Lab Technician
Accountable (A): QA Manager
Duration: 60-180 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task7" name="QA Lab Technician records test results in Oracle Quality (fit-gap C12) with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: QA Lab Technician records test results in Oracle Quality (fit-gap C12) with test method reference, equipment calibration date, environmental conditions (temperature, humidity), and pass/fail determination against specification
Responsible (R): QA Lab Technician
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task8" name="Pass">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pass: QA Manager reviews results; product cleared for DC putaway and store distribution; system updates item quality status to &quot;Tested — Passed&quot; with test date and expiry (retest due date)
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task9" name="Fail">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Fail: QA Manager initiates quality hold (per W110) — product quarantined at DC; Buyer notified; vendor contacted with test results and documentation; disposition options: (a) return to vendor (per W88), (b) vendor rework, (c) destroy per DENR compliance (per W82)
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): Buyer
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task10" name="Monthly: QA Manager reviews product certification tracker — DTI-BPS ICC/SOC…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly: QA Manager reviews product certification tracker — DTI-BPS ICC/SOC certificates (per W447), FDA product notifications (per W479), FPA registrations for pesticides/chemicals; verifies certificates are current for all active SKUs in regulated categories; system auto-alerts 60 days before certificate expiry
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task11" name="Monthly: QA Manager generates quality dashboard — test pass rate by vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly: QA Manager generates quality dashboard — test pass rate by vendor, test pass rate by category, certification compliance rate, customer quality complaint correlation, and corrective action status (per W110)
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W625_Task12" name="Quarterly: QA Manager and Category Manager review quality performance by…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Quarterly: QA Manager and Category Manager review quality performance by vendor; incorporates into vendor scorecard (per W44); identifies vendors requiring CAPA (per W110) or sourcing review (per W491)
Responsible (R): QA Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W625_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W625_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W625_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W625_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: prioritizing tests by risk level and outsourcing surge capacity to accredited third-party labs (SGS, Intertek); operational: annual calibration of lab equipment, participation in inter-laboratory comparison programs, and third-party verification of critical test results; operational: centralized certification tracker with automated expiry alerting
Owner: Quality Assurance Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W625_Assoc15" sourceRef="W625_Annotation14" targetRef="W625_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
