    <bpmn:process id="W_W1220" name="W1220. Seasonal Forward-Buy &amp; Pre-Season Stock Build Planning for Philippine Weather Cycles" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal planning calendar (6 months before season peak); or triggered by PAGASA long-range forecast indicating unusual weather patterns
Frequency: Forward-buy planning cycles aligned to W1422&#x27;s 6 seasonal events/year aligned with Philippine seasonal calendar: (a) Q1 plan (Jan–Mar) for summer/dry season, (b) Q2 plan (Apr–Jun) for rainy season, (c) Q3 plan (Jul–Sep) for typhoon peak and ber-months, (d) Q4 plan (Oct–Dec) for holiday/Christmas peak
Volume: ~500–800 seasonal SKUs per planning cycle; ~PHP 100–200M in forward-buy purchase orders per cycle (per W1422&#x27;s seasonal-investment canon)
Owner: Merchandise Planner
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Category Manager, Buyer, Supply Planning Analyst, VP Merchandising, Finance Manager
Source: workflow W1220 — Seasonal Forward-Buy &amp; Pre-Season Stock Build Planning for Philippine Weather Cycles</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1220_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1220_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1220_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1220_Lane3" name="Supply Planning Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1220_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1220_Start5" name="Seasonal planning calendar (6 months before season peak); or triggered by PAGASA…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1220_Task6" name="Seasonal demand planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal demand planning (T-6 months): Merchandise Planner develops seasonal demand forecast by category: (a) analyze prior year seasonal sales by SKU and category, (b) incorporate PAGASA long-range forecast (rainy season onset, typhoon predictions), (c) adjust for store count growth (10–15 new stores/year), (d) incorporate planned promotions per W13 seasonal calendar, (e) identify new seasonal SKU candidates for introduction, (f) generate seasonal buy plan: SKU-level quantities, target in-stock date, and target inventory level
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1220_Task7" name="Vendor capacity reservation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor capacity reservation (T-5 months): Buyer contacts seasonal vendors to reserve production capacity: (a) share preliminary seasonal demand forecast with top 20 seasonal vendors, (b) negotiate forward-buy pricing and volume discounts, (c) reserve production slots for import items (Chinese New Year factory closures in Jan–Feb affect Q2 delivery), (d) confirm import logistics: container space reservation, port of entry, customs broker capacity per W2B
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1220_Task8" name="Working capital and budget approval">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Working capital and budget approval (T-4 months): Merchandise Planner and Finance Manager prepare seasonal buy budget: (a) total seasonal inventory investment by category, (b) peak seasonal inventory value (maximum working capital tied up), (c) expected sell-through rate and margin, (d) markdown risk estimate (unsold seasonal inventory per W588), (e) VP Merchandising and CFO approve seasonal buy budget
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising / CFO
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1220_Task9" name="Purchase order placement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Purchase order placement (T-4 months for imports; T-2 months for local): Buyer places seasonal forward-buy POs: (a) import POs (45–90 day lead time) for Chinese/Taiwanese seasonal items: Christmas lights, garden furniture, flood control items, (b) local POs (7–21 day lead time) for Philippine-made seasonal items: paint, cement, roofing, (c) stagger delivery dates: early deliveries for season-start items, mid-season top-ups based on sell-through, (d) system tracks seasonal PO status separately from regular replenishment POs
Responsible (R): Buyer
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1220_Task10" name="Pre-season inventory build monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Pre-season inventory build monitoring (T-2 months to T-0): Supply Planning Analyst monitors seasonal inventory build: (a) weekly: track seasonal SKU on-order vs. target by DC, (b) identify late deliveries and expedite with vendor, (c) monitor DC capacity for seasonal storage — ensure seasonal inventory does not displace regular replenishment stock, (d) coordinate with DC Supervisor for pre-positioning of high-demand seasonal items (e.g., stage flood control items at Visayas/Mindanao DCs before typhoon season)
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week during build phase</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1220_Task11" name="In-season sell-through monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: In-season sell-through monitoring (T-0 to end of season): Merchandise Planner monitors weekly seasonal sell-through: (a) actual sales vs. forecast by SKU, (b) identify fast sellers requiring replenishment (if vendor capacity allows), (c) identify slow sellers requiring early markdown per W93 to clear before season end, (d) update forecast and adjust future seasonal orders, (e) weekly report to Category Manager with action recommendations
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2 hours/week during season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1220_Task12" name="End-of-season clearance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: End-of-season clearance (T-end of season): execute seasonal inventory wind-down per W588: (a) mark down remaining seasonal inventory per clearance schedule (week 1: 20% off, week 2: 30% off, week 3: 50% off, week 4: 70% off), (b) if remaining inventory still significant: consolidate to select stores for final clearance, (c) unsold seasonal items: evaluate for carry-forward to next year (if style/color still relevant) or liquidate per W220 SLOB process
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1220_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1220_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1220_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1220_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: Merchandise Planner review and approval gate
Owner: Merchandise Planner</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1220_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1220_Annotation14" targetRef="W1220_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1220_Flow16" sourceRef="W1220_Start5" targetRef="W1220_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1220_Flow17" sourceRef="W1220_Task6" targetRef="W1220_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1220_Flow18" sourceRef="W1220_Task7" targetRef="W1220_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1220_Flow19" sourceRef="W1220_Task8" targetRef="W1220_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1220_Flow20" sourceRef="W1220_Task9" targetRef="W1220_Task10" />
