    <bpmn:process id="W_W1265" name="W1265. Private Label Product Lifecycle Management, Quality Governance &amp; Brand Performance Analytics" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — quarterly private label portfolio review; annual brand performance assessment; ad-hoc triggered by quality failure, competitive threat, or new category entry opportunity
Frequency: Quarterly portfolio review; annual brand performance deep-dive; continuous quality monitoring
Volume: ~4,000–5,000 private label SKUs across the category range (hardware/fasteners, paint, tools, electrical fittings, plumbing fixtures, cleaning supplies, garden supplies; ~8–12% of the 35,000 active SKU count per W1513); representing ~5–8% of total revenue
Owner: Category Manager (Private Label)
Participants: VP Merchandising, Procurement Manager, Quality Assurance, Supplier (OEM), Finance Controller, Marketing Manager
Source: workflow W1265 — Private Label Product Lifecycle Management, Quality Governance &amp; Brand Performance Analytics</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1265_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1265_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1265_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1265_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1265_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1265_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1265_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1265_Lane2" name="Quality Assurance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1265_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1265_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1265_Start4" name="Scheduled — quarterly private label portfolio review; annual brand performance…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1265_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1265_Task5" name="Quarterly private label portfolio review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly private label portfolio review: Category Manager (Private Label) conducts quarterly review: (a) sales performance by category — private label revenue, gross margin, and sell-through rate vs. national brand benchmarks; (b) market share within BuildRight: private label % of category sales (target: 15–25% of category); (c) identify underperforming SKUs: private label with &lt; 60% sell-through rate or declining &gt; 10% QoQ; (d) identify expansion opportunities: national brand categories where private label is absent but margin opportunity exists; (e) present portfolio health scorecard to VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Category Manager (Private Label)
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1265_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1265_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1265_Task6" name="Quality governance &amp; supplier audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quality governance &amp; supplier audit: Quality Assurance conducts quarterly quality audit of private label OEM suppliers: (a) factory quality system audit per W160 — ISO 9001 compliance, incoming material QC, in-process QC, final inspection; (b) product quality testing per W625 — random sample testing of private label products: dimensional accuracy, material composition, durability, finish quality; (c) customer complaint analysis — warranty claims and product returns attributed to private label; target: defect rate &lt; 0.5%; (d) for recurring quality issues: issue corrective action request (CAR) to OEM supplier with 30-day remediation deadline; (e) for persistent quality failures: initiate supplier replacement — qualify new OEM per W160
Responsible (R): Quality Assurance / Procurement Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 16 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1265_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1265_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1265_Task7" name="Product lifecycle decisions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Product lifecycle decisions: Based on quarterly review, make lifecycle decisions per private label SKU: (a) Continue: performing at or above target — no action; (b) Improve: reformulate, redesign packaging, adjust price — execute within 90 days; (c) Replace: discontinue current SKU and introduce updated version with improved specs — manage per W68 (discontinuation) and W564 (NPI rollout); (d) Exit: discontinue private label in category where national brand dominance makes private label uncompetitive — phase out per W68 with sell-through plan; (e) document all lifecycle decisions with financial justification (margin impact, volume impact)
Responsible (R): Category Manager (Private Label)
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1265_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1265_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1265_Task8" name="Annual brand performance deep-dive">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Annual brand performance deep-dive: Annual comprehensive assessment: (a) total private label revenue and margin contribution vs. target; (b) brand awareness and perception survey among loyalty members; (c) competitive benchmarking — how do BuildRight private label prices and quality compare to national brands and competitor private labels?; (d) 3-year portfolio roadmap: which categories to enter, which to expand, which to exit; (e) packaging and brand refresh assessment — does the private label packaging design need updating?; (f) present annual private label strategy to CEO and VP Merchandising with investment proposals
Responsible (R): Category Manager (Private Label) / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: 24 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1265_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1265_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1265_Task9" name="Customer feedback integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer feedback integration: Continuous monitoring of customer feedback on private label products: (a) ecommerce product review analysis (per W510) — flag private label products with &lt; 3.5 star average rating; (b) in-store customer complaint analysis — recurring complaints about specific private label products; (c) trade professional feedback — contractor satisfaction with private label tools, hardware, and materials; (d) route feedback to Category Manager for product improvement or lifecycle decision
Responsible (R): Category Manager (Private Label) / Marketing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1265_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1265_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1265_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1265_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1265_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: Category Manager (Private Label) review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager (Private Label)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
