    <bpmn:process id="W_W1422" name="W1422. Seasonal Merchandise Forward Buy Planning, Import Pre-Booking &amp; Arrival Calendar Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal planning cycle (quarterly S&amp;OP); or vendor advance order discount offer; or 6-month seasonal merchandise calendar review
Frequency: Quarterly forward buy planning sessions; ongoing import pre-booking (45–90 days before seasonal need date)
Volume: 6 major seasonal events per year per Philippine seasonal calendar; ~500 seasonal SKUs requiring forward buy; ~20–30 import containers per seasonal event
Owner: VP Merchandising
Participants: VP Merchandising, Category Manager, Buyer, Supply Planning Manager, Import Coordinator, FP&amp;A Analyst
Source: workflow W1422 — Seasonal Merchandise Forward Buy Planning, Import Pre-Booking &amp; Arrival Calendar Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1422_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1422_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1422_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1422_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1422_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1422_Lane2" name="Buyer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1422_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1422_Lane3" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1422_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1422_Lane4" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1422_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1422_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1422_Start6" name="Seasonal planning cycle (quarterly S&amp;OP); or vendor advance order discount offer; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1422_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1422_Task7" name="Seasonal demand planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal demand planning (T-6 months): Category Manager develops seasonal demand plan for upcoming season: (a) historical sales analysis for same season last year (units sold, revenue, sell-through rate, markdown rate), (b) current year adjustments: (i) planned new stores opening before the season (higher aggregate demand), (ii) macro factors (e.g., above-average typhoon forecast increases waterproofing demand), (iii) vendor promotions and new product launches, (c) seasonal buy quantity = projected demand × (1 + safety buffer) − current inventory of seasonal items carried forward, (d) FP&amp;A Analyst reviews seasonal buy budget: total forward buy investment, target sell-through, and markdown provision
Responsible (R): Category Manager / FP&amp;A Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1422_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1422_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1422_Task8" name="Vendor negotiation and forward buy commitment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor negotiation and forward buy commitment (T-5 months): Buyer negotiates with vendors: (a) present seasonal demand forecast to key vendors, (b) negotiate: (i) volume discounts for forward commitment, (ii) consignment terms for high-risk seasonal items, (iii) vendor-funded promotional support (co-op advertising, display materials), (iv) return/exchange terms for unsold seasonal stock, (c) confirm production and shipping schedule with import vendors (45–90 day lead time), (d) VP Merchandising approves seasonal buy commitment (total seasonal investment typically PHP 100–200M per season across all categories)
Responsible (R): Buyer / VP Merchandising
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–5 days/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1422_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1422_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1422_Task9" name="Import pre-booking and logistics coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Import pre-booking and logistics coordination (T-4 months): Import Coordinator pre-books import shipments: (a) for each import vendor&#x27;s seasonal order: (i) book container space with shipping line (peak season: Jun–Aug and Sep–Nov container space is competitive in Philippine trade lanes), (ii) confirm estimated time of departure (ETD) and estimated time of arrival (ETA), (iii) coordinate with customs broker per W464 for pre-clearance documentation, (b) update seasonal arrival calendar: all seasonal import POs with expected arrival dates, (c) identify risk: POs with ETA after season start — expedite shipping (air freight for critical items) or push to next season
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator / Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1422_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1422_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1422_Task10" name="Arrival calendar monitoring and DC coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Arrival calendar monitoring and DC coordination (T-2 months to T-0): (a) Supply Planning Manager monitors arrival calendar weekly: track container ETAs against seasonal need dates, (b) coordinate with DC for receiving capacity: seasonal arrivals may require additional staging space per W652, (c) trigger promotional setup: Marketing team initiates seasonal promotional materials (signage, circular, digital campaigns) aligned with merchandise arrival per W14.1, (d) Store Operations team prepares seasonal display areas per planogram
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 hours/week during seasonal ramp</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1422_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1422_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1422_Task11" name="Post-season sell-through review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-season sell-through review: (a) Category Manager reviews seasonal sell-through within 2 weeks of season end: (i) units sold vs. planned, (ii) sell-through rate, (iii) markdown rate, (iv) gross margin after markdowns, (b) VP Merchandising conducts post-season review with Category Managers: what worked, what didn&#x27;t, lessons for next year&#x27;s seasonal plan, (c) update seasonal demand model with actual results for next year&#x27;s planning cycle
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4–6 hours/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1422_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1422_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1422_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1422_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1422_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: VP Merchandising review and approval gate
Owner: VP Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1422_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1422_Annotation13" targetRef="W1422_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1422_Flow15" sourceRef="W1422_Start6" targetRef="W1422_Task7" />
