    <bpmn:process id="W_W1487" name="W1487. Store Garden Center &amp; Plant Nursery Seasonal Assortment Rotation, Vendor-Managed Inventory &amp; Markdown Optimization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal assortment review cycle (quarterly); also triggered when plant nursery sell-through rate drops below 60% or spoilage rate exceeds 15% for any SKU category
Frequency: Quarterly major rotation; monthly performance review; weekly markdown trigger assessment
Volume: ~50–120 live plant SKUs per store with garden center (by tier: large 120 / medium 80 / small 50, per step 1e); spoilage-sensitive items represent ~30% of garden center revenue; ~200 stores with garden-center/outdoor-yard areas (per VS-145)
Owner: Category Manager (Outdoor &amp; Garden)
Participants: Store Garden Center Associate, Merchandise Planner, Vendor Account Manager, Department Supervisor
Source: workflow W1487 — Store Garden Center &amp; Plant Nursery Seasonal Assortment Rotation, Vendor-Managed Inventory &amp; Markdown Optimization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1487_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1487_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1487_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1487_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1487_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1487_Lane2" name="Vendor Account Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1487_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1487_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1487_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1487_Lane4" name="Garden Center Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1487_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1487_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1487_Start6" name="Seasonal assortment review cycle (quarterly); also triggered when plant nursery…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1487_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1487_Task7" name="Quarterly seasonal assortment review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly seasonal assortment review: Quarterly: (a) Category Manager reviews sell-through rates by species/category for the past quarter; (b) underperforming SKUs (sell-through &lt; 50%) flagged for discontinuation or replacement; (c) seasonal rotation planned: (i) dry season (Dec–May): drought-tolerant succulents, cacti, flowering bougainvillea, herb gardens; (ii) rainy season (Jun–Nov): water-loving ferns, aquatic plants, mushroom logs, indoor air-purifying plants; (d) new variety introductions sourced from vendor catalog; (e) assortment plan finalized with target SKU count per store tier (large garden centers: 120 SKUs; medium: 80; small: 50)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1487_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1487_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1487_Task8" name="Vendor-managed inventory (VMI) for live plants">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor-managed inventory (VMI) for live plants: (a) major plant vendors (nurseries in Davao, Laguna, Cebu) replenish stores on a VMI basis; (b) vendors access store-level sales and inventory data through BuildRight vendor portal; (c) vendors generate replenishment orders based on agreed min/max levels and sell-through velocity; (d) Merchandise Planner approves/rejects vendor-proposed replenishment quantities; (e) vendor delivers fresh stock on scheduled route (typically weekly or bi-weekly per store cluster); (f) vendor removes unsellable/spoiled plants during delivery visit and issues credit memo
Responsible (R): Vendor Account Manager / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1487_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1487_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1487_Task9" name="Progressive markdown for aging plants">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Progressive markdown for aging plants: Weekly: (a) system tracks days-since-receipt for each live plant SKU; (b) progressive markdown schedule applied: (i) week 1–2: full price; (ii) week 3: 15% markdown; (iii) week 4: 30% markdown; (iv) week 5: 50% markdown; (v) week 6+: write-off or donate to community garden program per PA-25.2; (c) markdown labels auto-generated for store associates to apply; (d) markdown effectiveness (sell-through improvement) tracked per category; (e) Category Manager reviews markdown performance monthly to adjust thresholds
Responsible (R): System / Garden Center Associate
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week per store</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1487_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1487_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1487_Task10" name="Daily plant care &amp; condition monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Daily plant care &amp; condition monitoring: Daily: (a) Garden Center Associate waters all plants per species-specific schedule; (b) removes dead leaves, damaged flowers, and pest-infested plants; (c) rotates sun-sensitive plants to shade during peak heat (11am–2pm in dry season); (d) moves rain-sensitive container plants under cover during heavy rainfall; (e) applies pest control treatment for observed infestations (aphids, mealybugs, fungus gnats); (f) logs plant condition observations in system for trend analysis
Responsible (R): Garden Center Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 60–90 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1487_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1487_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1487_Task11" name="Garden center seasonal event promotions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Garden center seasonal event promotions: Aligned with key gardening seasons: (a) January–February: &quot;New Year Garden Makeover&quot; promo — bundle discounts on soil + fertilizer + seedlings; (b) June–July: &quot;Rainy Season Planting&quot; — focus on indoor plants and drainage solutions; (c) September: &quot;Ber Months Landscaping&quot; — landscape-ready shrubs and trees for Christmas garden prep; (d) Category Manager coordinates with Marketing per PA-14.1 for promotional execution; (e) vendor co-op funding negotiated per PA-03.3 for promotional plants
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1487_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1487_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1487_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1487_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1487_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: Category Manager (Outdoor &amp; Garden) review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager (Outdoor &amp; Garden)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1487_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1487_Annotation13" targetRef="W1487_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1487_Flow15" sourceRef="W1487_Start6" targetRef="W1487_Task7" />
