    <bpmn:process id="W_W1513" name="W1513. Private Label Supplier Performance Scorecard, Quality Audit &amp; Range Refresh Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly private label review cycle or quality incident from customer complaint (W795)
Frequency: Quarterly scorecard reviews; annual range refresh
Volume: ~15–20 private label suppliers across paint, hand tools, electrical fittings, plumbing fixtures, and hardware lines
Owner: Category Manager (Private Label)
Participants: Category Manager, Quality Assurance Specialist, Sourcing Manager, Merchandise Planner, Finance Controller
Source: workflow W1513 — Private Label Supplier Performance Scorecard, Quality Audit &amp; Range Refresh Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1513_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1513_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1513_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1513_Lane3" name="Sourcing Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1513_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1513_Start5" name="Quarterly private label review cycle or quality incident from customer complaint (W795)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1513_Task6" name="Quarterly scorecard compilation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Quarterly scorecard compilation: System aggregates supplier performance data for each private label supplier: (a) quality metrics: defect rate (PPM), customer return rate, BIR/DENR compliance status; (b) delivery metrics: on-time-in-full (OTIF), lead time adherence, expedited order fulfillment rate; (c) commercial metrics: cost competitiveness vs. national brand benchmark, margin contribution, rebate achievement; (d) responsiveness: sample lead time, complaint resolution time, flexibility on order quantity changes
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/supplier</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1513_Task7" name="Category Manager reviews scorecard; rates each supplier Green / Yellow / Red…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Manager reviews scorecard; rates each supplier Green / Yellow / Red across four dimensions; flags suppliers with two or more Yellow ratings or any Red rating for remediation discussion
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 hour/supplier</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1513_Task8" name="Annual product quality audit">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Annual product quality audit: (a) Category Manager and QA Specialist visit supplier factory (or commission third-party audit for overseas suppliers); (b) audit covers: raw material sourcing, production process controls, finished goods inspection procedures, packaging quality, storage conditions, labor compliance (DOLE standards for Philippine suppliers); (c) audit score documented in supplier master with findings and corrective actions
Responsible (R): Category Manager / QA Specialist
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days per supplier visit</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1513_Task9" name="Range refresh assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Range refresh assessment: (a) Merchandise Planner analyzes private label SKU performance: sell-through rate, margin contribution, cannibalization of national brand equivalent; (b) Category Manager identifies: (i) SKUs to discontinue (poor sell-through &lt; 30% in 6 months), (ii) SKUs to refresh (updated packaging, improved formulation/spec), (iii) new SKUs to add (gap analysis vs. competitor private label ranges); (c) cross-reference with W1 (Merchandise Planning) and W64 (New Product Pilot)
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1513_Task10" name="For SKUs requiring refresh: Sourcing Manager coordinates with supplier on…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: For SKUs requiring refresh: Sourcing Manager coordinates with supplier on reformulation or specification upgrade; samples produced and tested per W625 (Quality Lab Testing); updated cost negotiated
Responsible (R): Sourcing Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–4 weeks lead time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1513_Task11" name="Category Manager presents quarterly private label portfolio performance and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Category Manager presents quarterly private label portfolio performance and range refresh recommendations to VP Merchandising for approval; Finance Controller validates margin impact
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1513_Task12" name="Approved changes executed: discontinued SKUs routed to W68 (Product Lifecycle &amp;…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Approved changes executed: discontinued SKUs routed to W68 (Product Lifecycle &amp; Discontinuation) and W830 (Phase-Out Disposition); new SKUs follow W564 (NPI); refreshed SKUs updated in product master with new specifications, costs, and transition timeline
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 weeks execution</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1513_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1513_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1513_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1513_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-240 (ensure controlled execution — Assortment Planning &amp; Product Lifecycle (PA-01.1).) | - operational: Category Manager (Private Label) review and approval gate
Owner: Category Manager (Private Label)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1513_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1513_Annotation14" targetRef="W1513_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1513_Flow16" sourceRef="W1513_Start5" targetRef="W1513_Task6" />
